    <!--
        Family Notification: body of the automated SMS sent to the emergency contact.

        MEASURED COST: 157 characters = 159 GSM-7 septets. Limit for a single SMS is 160 septets,
        so this fits in ONE message with only 1 septet of headroom.

        WARNING - two separate traps when editing this string:
        1. '[' and ']' are GSM-7 EXTENSION characters costing 2 septets each, not 1. That is why
           157 characters cost 159 septets. Adding even two more plain characters splits this into
           2 billed parts.
        2. Any emoji, curly quote, em dash or accented letter forces the entire body to UCS-2,
           collapsing the limit from 160 to 70 septets and turning this into 3 parts.
        Keep edits inside the GSM-7 basic alphabet and re-measure septets, not characters.
    -->
    <!--
      MUST stay GSM-7 and under 160 characters = ONE SMS segment.
      Every character here is plain ASCII on purpose. A single emoji (a shield, a warning sign)
      switches the whole message to UCS-2, which drops the segment size from 160 to 67 characters
      and turns this one message into THREE billed segments on every emergency, forever.
      The branding is therefore carried by the uppercase header, not by an icon.

      Note the SENDER NAME is NOT settable from the app: SmsManager always sends from the SIM's own
      number, and the recipient's phone displays whatever name it has saved for it. An alphanumeric
      sender ID would require a paid SMS gateway, which this project deliberately does not use.
      This header is what makes the message identifiably from Aegis Drive.
    -->
    <string name="family_alert_message">AEGIS DRIVE - SAFETY ALERT: The driver has triggered critical drowsiness alerts and may be falling asleep. Please contact them immediately.</string>

